(ns kotoba.lang.error
  "The host's ex-info exception class under a kotoba name, so a `.cljk` call
  site never has to spell `clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo` (a JVM class name) to
  catch, test for, or assert on an `ex-info`.

    (catch err/ExceptionInfo e ..)            ; was (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e ..)
    (is (thrown? err/ExceptionInfo ..))       ; was (thrown? clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo ..)
    (is (thrown-with-msg? err/ExceptionInfo #\"..\" ..))
    (err/ex-info? x)                          ; was (instance? clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo x)

  `ExceptionInfo` IS the host class (the object, not a copy or a wrapper):
  clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo on the JVM, cljs.core/ExceptionInfo on the kbb
  engine / ClojureScript. So `ex-info?` answers exactly what
  `(instance? clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo x)` answers on the same host, and a
  catch clause naming it catches exactly the throwables the old clause caught
  -- on hosts where a catch clause's class position is an evaluated
  expression.

  THE BOUNDARY (why this is not a JVM drop-in). On the kbb engine (SCI) and in
  ClojureScript the class position of `catch` / `thrown?` /
  `thrown-with-msg?` is evaluated, so the var works there. JVM Clojure's
  compiler resolves that position as a CLASS LITERAL at compile time; a var
  (`err/ExceptionInfo`) is `Unable to resolve classname` there. `.cljk` is
  loaded only by the kbb engine (ADR-2609111700), which is what this
  namespace is for; a JVM `.clj` / `.cljc` source keeps
  `clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo` (or a reader conditional) in catch position.
  `ex-info?` has no such limit -- it is a function on every host.

  Not the same question as `(some? (ex-data e))`: that is true of any
  IExceptionInfo, and on ClojureScript false for `(ex-info msg nil)`, whose
  ex-data stays nil (the JVM, Clojure 1.12, stores {} instead -- measured).
  `ex-info?` asks about the class, as the call sites it replaces did.

  (No `:kotoba/export` attr-map: the JVM `ns` macro EVALUATES that map, and a
  vector of not-yet-defined symbols is `Unable to resolve symbol` there --
  measured, and this namespace is loaded on the JVM as the oracle's host.)")

(def ExceptionInfo
  "The host's ex-info class: clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo on the JVM,
  cljs.core/ExceptionInfo on the kbb engine / ClojureScript."
  )

(defn ex-info?
  "True when `x` is an instance of the host's ex-info class -- what
  `(instance? clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo x)` answers on the JVM and
  `(instance? ExceptionInfo x)` in ClojureScript. False for nil and for any
  other throwable."
  [x]
  (instance? ExceptionInfo x))
